s using the link script `$WALLY/tests/riscof/spike/env/link.ld` and HTIF `.tohost` section:\n1. `test_zacas_rd1_hazard.S` (Bug Reproducer):\n   - Initialize 16-byte memory at `test_val` with `{low: 42, high: 777}` (aligned to 16 bytes).\n   - Load address into `a0`.\n   - Set `a2 = 42`, `a3 = 100`, `a4 = 99`, `a5 = 999`.\n   - Execute `amocas.q a2, a4, (a0)`.\n     - Since `a2:a3` ({42, 100}) does not match memory ({42, 777}), `amocas.q` loads `{42, 777}` into `a2:a3`, updating `a3` to 777.\n   - Immediately follow with a RAW consumer of `a3`: `addi a6, a3, 0` (0 NOP distance) or with 1 NOP distance.\n   - Compare `a6` with 777. If `a6 == 777`, jump to `pass` (write 1 to `tohost`, loop `1: j 1b`). If `a6 != 777` (stale value 100), jump to `fail` (`csrw mtvec, x0; jr x0`).\n2. `test_zacas_rd1_control.S` (Positive Control):\n   - Identical to `test_zacas_rd1_hazard.S`, but inserts 3 `nop` instructions between `amocas.q` and `addi a6, a3, 0`.\n   - This allows `amocas.q` to pass through Writeback and commit `a3` to `regfile.sv` on `negedge clk`, ensuring `addi` reads 777.\n3. `test_zacas_rd0_hazard.S` (Negative Control):\n   - Tests base register `a2` (`rd`) back-to-back (`amocas.q` followed immediately by `addi a6, a2, 0`), ensuring existing hazard/forwarding logic for `rd` remains intact.\n\n### 4. Reproducer Script Contract (`$TEST_DIR/reproducer.sh`)\n- The script must build all ELF binaries into `$TEST_DIR/build/`.\n- Run Spike oracle on all tests with `timeout 5s`. Ensure Spike passes with exit code 0. If Spike fails, exit 2.\n- Run Wally DUT (`Vtestbench`) on `test_zacas_rd1_control.elf`. It must pass cleanly (exit 0). If it fails, exit 2.\n- Run Wally DUT on `test_zacas_rd1_hazard.elf`. Log output to `$TEST_DIR/logs/hazard.log`.\n- Detect the functional mismatch:\n  - If DUT fails (exit code 134, or log contains 'Assertion failed in testbench: Program fetched illegal instruction 0x00000000 twice in a row' or 'Watch Dog Time Out triggered'), exit 1.\n  - If DUT 